Build a simple ascii chart from OHLCV cl.ts:
Fetch hourly candles with `fetchOHLCV`, scale each close between the min and max, and draw one row of `#` per candle.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.binance();
const candles = await exchange.fetchOHLCV('BTC/USDT', '1h', undefined, 24);
const closes = candles.map((c) => c[4] ?? 0);
const min = Math.min(...closes);
const max = Math.max(...closes);
const width = 50;
