Fetch closed orders and compute the real.ts:
Fetch closed orders with `fetchClosedOrders` and estimate realized PnL as sell proceeds minus buy cost minus fees (from each order's `cost` and `fee`). This only holds when the window opens and closes flat, because it ignores any position held before it.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.bybit({ apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY', secret: 'YOUR_SECRET' });
const symbol = 'BTC/USDT';
const orders = await exchange.fetchClosedOrders(symbol);
let pnl = 0;
for (const order of orders) {
    const cost = order.cost ?? 0;
    pnl += order.side === 'sell' ? cost : -cost;
    pnl -= order.fee?.cost ?? 0;
}
console.log(`Closed orders: ${orders.length}, realized PnL: ${pnl}`);
```

