Fetch closed orders and compute the real.java:
Fetch closed orders with `fetchClosedOrders` and estimate realized PnL as sell proceeds minus buy cost minus fees (from each order's `cost` and `fee`). This only holds when the window opens and closes flat, because it ignores any position held before it.

```java
import io.github.ccxt.exchanges.Bybit;
import io.github.ccxt.types.Order;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Map<String, Object> config = new HashMap<>();
        config.put("apiKey", "YOUR_API_KEY");
        config.put("secret", "YOUR_SECRET");
        Bybit exchange = new Bybit(config);
        List<Order> orders = exchange.fetchClosedOrders("BTC/USDT");
        double pnl = 0;
        for (Order order : orders) {
            double cost = order.cost != null ? order.cost : 0.0;
            pnl += "sell".equals(order.side) ? cost : -cost;
            if (order.fee != null && order.fee.cost != null) {
                pnl -= order.fee.cost;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Closed orders: " + orders.size() + ", realized PnL: " + pnl);
    }
}
```

