Do a margin loan buy sell and repay cycl.ts:
Kraken has no explicit borrow/repay endpoints (`borrowMargin`/`repayMargin` are unsupported), so the loan is implicit: a `createOrder` with a `leverage` param opens a margin buy funded by borrowed quote currency, and the opposite `sell` with the same leverage closes the position and repays the loan.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.kraken({ apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY', secret: 'YOUR_SECRET' });
await exchange.loadMarkets();

const symbol = 'ETH/USDT';
const amount = exchange.market(symbol).limits.amount?.min ?? 0.01;
const params = { leverage: 2 };

// 1. margin buy: Kraken lends the rest of the USDT needed at 2x
const buy = await exchange.createOrder(symbol, 'market', 'buy', amount, undefined, params);
console.log('margin buy:', buy.id, buy.status);

// 2. inspect the open margin position (the outstanding loan)
const positions = await exchange.fetchPositions(undefined, { docalcs: true });
for (const p of positions) {
    console.log('position:', p.symbol, p.side, p.contracts);
}

// 3. sell with the same leverage: closes the position and repays the loan
const sell = await exchange.createOrder(symbol, 'market', 'sell', amount, undefined, params);
console.log('closing sell (repay):', sell.id, sell.status);

const balance = await exchange.fetchBalance();
console.log('USDT total after repay:', balance['USDT']?.total ?? 0);
```

