Watch orders and cancel any that stay op.ts:
Loop on `watchOrders` for okx, and whenever an update shows an order still `open` longer than a max age (from its `timestamp`), cancel it with `cancelOrder` (private, so dummy keys are used). Note the check only runs when an order update arrives; for a strict timeout, also poll on a timer.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.pro.okx({ apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY', secret: 'YOUR_SECRET', password: 'YOUR_PASSWORD' });
const maxAgeMs = 60 * 1000; // cancel orders open longer than 60 seconds
const cancelled = new Set<string>();
try {
    while (true) {
        const orders = await exchange.watchOrders();
        const now = exchange.milliseconds();
        for (const order of orders) {
            const id = order.id;
            if (id === undefined || order.status !== 'open' || cancelled.has(id)) continue;
            const age = now - (order.timestamp ?? now);
            if (age > maxAgeMs) {
                console.log(`Cancelling ${id} ${order.symbol} open for ${Math.round(age / 1000)}s`);
                await exchange.cancelOrder(id, order.symbol);
                cancelled.add(id);
            }
        }
    }
} catch (e) {
    console.log('Error:', e);
} finally {
    await exchange.close();
}
```

