Watch only new trades and skip the initi.ts:
With `newUpdates: true` (the ccxt default), each `watchTrades` call returns only trades received since the previous call; the first call's result (the warm-up batch) is thrown away, so only trades that arrive after you subscribe get printed.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.pro.binance({ newUpdates: true });
const symbol = 'BTC/USDT';

// first call subscribes and returns the initial batch: skip it
await exchange.watchTrades(symbol);

for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    const trades = await exchange.watchTrades(symbol);
    for (const t of trades) {
        console.log(t.datetime, t.side, t.price, t.amount);
    }
}
await exchange.close();
```

