Fetch an event on polymarket and then fe.ts:
Find an event with `fetchEvents` (scoped by `query`), re-fetch it by id with `fetchEvent`, then pass the first unresolved market's outcome handle (`outcome.outcome`) to `fetchTicker`; the price is the market-implied probability.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.prediction.polymarket();
const found = await exchange.fetchEvents({ query: 'bitcoin', sort: 'volume', limit: 1 });
if (found.length === 0 || found[0].id === undefined) {
    throw new Error('no event found');
}
const event = await exchange.fetchEvent(found[0].id);
console.log('event:', event.id, event.title);
const market = (event.markets ?? []).find((m) => !m.resolved && (m.outcomes ?? []).length > 0);
const outcome = market?.outcomes[0];
if (market === undefined || outcome === undefined || outcome.outcome === undefined) {
    throw new Error('no open market with outcomes in this event');
}
try {
    const ticker = await exchange.fetchTicker(outcome.outcome);
    console.log('market:', market.title);
    console.log('outcome:', outcome.label, 'last:', ticker.last, 'bid:', ticker.bid, 'ask:', ticker.ask);
} catch (e) {
    console.log('fetchTicker failed:', e instanceof Error ? e.message : e);
}
```

