Fetch tickers from many exchanges concur.ts:
Start every `fetchTicker` call at once and wait for all of them with `Promise.all` (each failure is caught so one bad exchange doesn't reject the batch); the other languages use their native equivalent — a thread pool in Python, ccxt's async classes with ReactPHP's `all()` in PHP, goroutines in Go, `Task.WhenAll` in C# and `CompletableFuture.allOf` in Java.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';
import type { Exchange } from 'ccxt';

const symbol = 'BTC/USDT';
const exchanges: Exchange[] = [new ccxt.binance(), new ccxt.okx(), new ccxt.bybit(), new ccxt.kucoin(), new ccxt.gate()];

const results = await Promise.all(
    exchanges.map(async (exchange) => {
        try {
            const ticker = await exchange.fetchTicker(symbol);
            return `${exchange.id.padEnd(10)} last ${ticker.last ?? 0}`;
        } catch (e) {
            return `${exchange.id.padEnd(10)} error: ${(e as Error).message}`;
        }
    }),
);
console.log(results.join('\n'));
```

