Validate that paginated OHLCV has no gap.ts:
Fetch several days of 1h candles from gate with `fetchOHLCV` and the `paginate: true` param, then check that consecutive timestamps differ by exactly one timeframe (`parseTimeframe` × 1000 ms) and report any gaps or duplicates.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.gate();
const timeframe = '1h';
const step = exchange.parseTimeframe(timeframe) * 1000;
const since = exchange.milliseconds() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
const candles = await exchange.fetchOHLCV('BTC/USDT', timeframe, since, undefined, { paginate: true });

let gaps = 0;
for (let i = 1; i < candles.length; i++) {
    const prev = candles[i - 1][0] ?? 0;
    const curr = candles[i][0] ?? 0;
    if (curr - prev !== step) {
        gaps++;
        console.log(`gap/overlap between ${exchange.iso8601(prev)} and ${exchange.iso8601(curr)} (${(curr - prev) / step} steps)`);
    }
}
console.log(`${candles.length} candles, ${gaps} problems`);
console.log(gaps === 0 ? 'OK: no gaps' : 'FAILED: series has gaps');
```

