Retry on RateLimitExceeded with exponent.ts:
Wrap the call in a loop that catches `RateLimitExceeded` and sleeps with exponentially growing delays (1s, 2s, 4s, ...) before retrying, giving up after five attempts.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';

const exchange = new ccxt.binance();
const maxRetries = 5;

for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {
    try {
        const ticker = await exchange.fetchTicker('BTC/USDT');
        console.log('last price:', ticker.last ?? 0);
        break;
    } catch (e) {
        if (e instanceof ccxt.RateLimitExceeded && attempt < maxRetries - 1) {
            const delay = 1000 * 2 ** attempt;
            console.log(`rate limited, retrying in ${delay} ms`);
            await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, delay));
        } else {
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
```

