Cache loadMarkets to a file and reuse it.ts:
Save `exchange.markets` to `markets.json` after the first `loadMarkets`, then give a fresh exchange instance those markets with `setMarkets` so it skips the network request.

```typescript
import ccxt from 'ccxt';
import { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'fs';

const cacheFile = 'markets.json';

if (!existsSync(cacheFile)) {
    const exchange = new ccxt.binance();
    await exchange.loadMarkets();
    writeFileSync(cacheFile, JSON.stringify(exchange.markets));
    console.log('Saved', Object.keys(exchange.markets ?? {}).length, 'markets to', cacheFile);
}

// later: reuse the cached markets without calling the API
const cached = new ccxt.binance();
cached.setMarkets(JSON.parse(readFileSync(cacheFile, 'utf8')));
console.log('Loaded from cache:', cached.market('BTC/USDT').id);
```

